# Requests for the VS Code "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client).
# Start the API first: `npm run dev` in backend/. Click "Send Request" above each block.
# Send both login requests first: the requests below reuse their tokens.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8888
@password = Password123!
# Filled from the login responses below (send those first):
@requesterToken = {{loginRequester.response.body.token}}
@validatorToken = {{loginValidator.response.body.token}}

### Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### Login as a requester (Alice)
# @name loginRequester
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "alice@example.com",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### Login as the validator
# @name loginValidator
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "validator@example.com",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### Current user — requester (what the frontend calls after a page reload)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{requesterToken}}

### Current user — validator
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{validatorToken}}


### --- Error cases ---

### 401: wrong password
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "alice@example.com",
  "password": "wrong"
}

### 401: unknown email — same answer as a wrong password
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "nobody@example.com",
  "password": "wrong"
}

### 400: invalid body (bad email, missing password)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "not-an-email"
}

### 401: no token
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me

### 401: forged token
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer not.a.real.token

### 404: unknown route
GET {{baseUrl}}/does-not-exist
